00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.620
And then they just wanted to
ideally form a joint opinion

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.710
or what the status is.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.730
And then based on this
view, then of course,

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.640
also proceed with all the invoicing.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:21.520
And they called these
meetings, thermometer meetings.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.000
I think that's also an interesting name.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.060
And all these projected profits

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.740
were supposed to be calculated

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:31.160
against agreed upon baselines,
not actual profits realized.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.870
This whole idea of building baselines

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.050
is also an important one,

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:35.830
because this is often also especially,

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:37.900
in the beginning of these
transformation programs,

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:38.733
something that

00:10:38.733 --> 00:10:41.180
at least the one associate
will often be concerned with.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:42.260
And here, the idea really is that

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.700
that this person often just tries

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.349
to develop different scenarios.

00:10:45.349 --> 00:10:46.977
So, tries to develop a scenario,

00:10:46.977 --> 00:10:49.730
what would happen if
nothing would happen, right?

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:51.166
So if no measure would be taken,

00:10:51.166 --> 00:10:54.310
if just business continues as usual,

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:57.560
how does maybe then the situation
of the company look like

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.050
in one year from now?

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.030
And this is then the baseline.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:02.580
And then against this baseline,

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.341
you the measure all the
financial improvements.

00:11:05.341 --> 00:11:07.493
And then of course, based on that,

00:11:07.493 --> 00:11:08.728
you can also develop scenarios,

00:11:08.728 --> 00:11:09.823
so based on the effect
of all the measures,

00:11:10.734 --> 00:11:12.420
sometimes of course the
baselines are not constant,

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.460
but deteriorating, right?

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.490
So imagine a company
where profits were down,

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.290
year over year, over year.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.910
Of course us on this baseline
will go into the negative

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:20.910
for the next year, right?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.360
So what you will say is
that if we do nothing,

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:26.330
next year profits will be,
let's say just a random number,

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.652
a hundred million less
than last year, right?

00:11:29.652 --> 00:11:31.904
And now of course, any profit improvement

00:11:31.904 --> 00:11:34.950
you can calculate on top of this baseline.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.530
But what this also means is
that even though, if you have,

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.474
or if you stand or realize 100 million

00:11:39.474 --> 00:11:42.690
in initiatives and profit
improvement initiatives,

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.460
this would just leave
the company's bottom line

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:46.970
just with no change, right?

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.640
Just with the zero data
compared to the last year,

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:50.980
because you're not necessarily measuring

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.080
against the last year,

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.077
but you're measuring against
the deteriorating baseline.

00:11:55.077 --> 00:11:57.230
And of course this isn't
something that maybe

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.766
not always managers really realize,

00:11:59.766 --> 00:12:01.063
if they put this together

00:12:01.063 --> 00:12:02.674
with with the help of
these consulting firms.

00:12:02.674 --> 00:12:04.869
And then of course they expect big jumps,

00:12:04.869 --> 00:12:05.702
big increases in profit.

00:12:05.702 --> 00:12:07.791
And then of course you'll often have

00:12:07.791 --> 00:12:08.865
these difficult situations,

00:12:08.865 --> 00:12:09.698
where the consulting firms claim, oh,

00:12:10.998 --> 00:12:12.770
you know, realize like all
these great profit improvements,

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.951
but then the company's just
looking at the bottom line,

00:12:15.951 --> 00:12:17.078
comparing one year with the other,

00:12:17.078 --> 00:12:17.950
seeing there's actually no change at all,

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.430
and then just wondering what
exactly happened here, right,

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.590
what the work of the
consulting firm has brought us.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.870
I think this logic of
measuring against the baseline

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:28.210
is not wrong, but of course
not always easy to communicate

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:30.910
in these dispute type of situations.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:32.510
So you can see that, you
know, what is, I mean,

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.910
what is BCG claiming that GameStop failed,

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:37.230
and refuse to pay BCG, that if they paid,

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.450
they they paid late, that here,

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.700
the CFO demanded all types
of unsupported reductions

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.250
to BCG fees,

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.910
that they just ceased to attend
these thermometer meetings.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.341
I mean, that's of course also a strategy.

00:12:48.341 --> 00:12:50.680
If you just don't attend
these meetings anymore,

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.870
then BCG doesn't have any
bases of going to you,

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.170
and trying to charge you
for these cost improvements.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.810
That's apparently what
they tried to do here.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.270
This, this is what BCG claims
again, no idea, of course,

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.354
whether this is correct or not.

00:13:01.354 --> 00:13:02.986
And here they're just saying, you know,

00:13:02.986 --> 00:13:05.130
unpaid fees of approximately 30 millions.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.669
This is what they want to have.

00:13:06.669 --> 00:13:07.947
And the interesting thing
they're also saying,

00:13:07.947 --> 00:13:10.597
"The exact amount of
the very fees own to BCG

00:13:10.597 --> 00:13:12.517
"is undetermined at this time,

00:13:12.517 --> 00:13:14.817
"due to GameStop's refusal
to hold thermometer meetings,

00:13:14.817 --> 00:13:17.547
"or otherwise furnish the data necessary

00:13:17.547 --> 00:13:19.410
"to determine certain
profit improvements."

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:20.620
That's exactly the problem, right?

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.450
So if you just stop attending this meeting

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.130
then of course you don't
have any issues here.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.110
So that's really the gist
of what's happening here.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.360
I must say, when I read all this

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.440
I did find this to be quite interesting.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.360
I hope you feel the very same way.

